{"segment_id":"R52-024","code":"speculative-cosmetic-edit","aspect":"intent","quote":"`/js/app.js` (absolute path from root) might not work in some Chrome versions for popups, usually it's `js/app.js` (relative).","memo":"Unverified belief drives an unnecessary popup.html edit; 'might not work' is hedged, no evidence. locus: agent","proposed_definition":"Agent applies an edit justified only by 'might be safer' hedging about unverified browser behaviour, changing a working reference."}
{"segment_id":"R52-024","code":"csp-empty-object-speculation","aspect":"agent-reasoning","quote":"If it's just `{}`, it might be ignored or might cause an error.","memo":"Agent speculates about empty CSP object then removes it 'just to be clean' without evidence it was harmful. locus: agent","proposed_definition":"Agent removes converter-emitted manifest field based on aesthetic cleanliness plus unverifiable error speculation rather than a documented MV3 violation."}
